<title>AZERBAIJAN: Azeri T-bill yield falls to 21.04 pct at auction.</title>
<headline>Azeri T-bill yield falls to 21.04 pct at auction.</headline>
<dateline>BAKU 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on the third issue of Azerbaijan's Treasury Bills fell sharply to 21.04 percent at Thursday's auction from 32.09 percent at the previous auction on October 21, a National Bank official said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction</p>
<p>						  Nov 21	     Oct 21</p>
<p> Issue volume (manats)...............13 bln...........11 bln</p>
<p> Denominations............... ........1 million............1 million</p>
<p> Average price (pct of face value)....98.30............97.43</p>
<p> Lowest accepted price................98.17............97.34</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)..................21.04............32.09</p>
<p> Highest accepted yield...............22.68............33.22</p>
<p> Maturity date........................Dec 20...........Nov 20</p>
<p>The official did not say how many T-bills were placed.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
